; A 20 x 10 x 2 conductor (k 200, x 0..20) held at 20 C over its first 0.01 mm, 1 W
; spread over its last millimetre (x 19..20), with an insulating layer (k 0.2) 0.02 mm
; thick across it at x 9.07..9.09. Every datum is uniform over
; the section and the other faces are insulated, so it is exactly one-dimensional.
; truth: cool fails about 29.8675 (1-D series resistance: the layer, 0.02 mm / (0.2 W/(m K) x 20 mm2) = 5.0 K/W; the conductor from the held band to the source, (18.99 - 0.02) mm / (200 W/(m K) x 20 mm2), and half the source's millimetre, 4.8675 K/W; 20 + 1 W x their sum)
; truth: warm holds about 29.8675 (as cool)
(import "std")
(def part (move (box 20 10 2) 10 0 0))
(def pad (max (- 9.07 x) (- x 9.09)))
(study hot (shape part) (heat (k (* 1W/m/K (select pad 0.2 200))))
 (temperature cold (- x 0.01) 20degC)
 (source chip (power 1W) (region (- 19 x))))
(require cool (max-temperature hot < 27degC))
(require warm (max-temperature hot > 27degC))
